---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Layout
  title="About Gantt Charter"
  description="Gantt Charter is a free, open-source tool for print-quality project timelines, created by Sami Adnan. Learn about the project and how to contribute."
>
  <SiteHeader current="about" />
  <main class="doc">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Gantt Charter makes project timelines that are good enough to print: in a thesis, a grant
      application, a report. It is free, open source, and runs entirely in your browser.
    </p>

    <p>
      Created by <strong>Sami Adnan</strong>
      (<a href="https://github.com/sami5001" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">@sami5001</a> on GitHub),
      University of Oxford. The project began as a Python command-line tool for generating
      publication-quality Gantt charts with Plotly and the Oxford colour palettes; this web app is
      its browser-native companion. Both share the same CSV template and YAML schema, so a project
      file moves freely between them.
    </p>
    <p>
      The chart engine is a small, dependency-free SVG renderer written for print discipline:
      hairline gridlines, direct labels, restrained ink. One rendering path drives the on-screen
      preview and every export, so the PDF you hand in is exactly the preview you saw.
    </p>

    <h2>Contributing</h2>
    <p>Contributions of every size are welcome. The short version:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Found a bug or have an idea?</strong>
        <a href="https://github.com/sami5001/gantt-charter/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open a GitHub issue</a>.
        For bugs, include what you did, what you expected, and (if you can) a CSV or YAML file that reproduces it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Want to change code?</strong> Fork the
        <a href="https://github.com/sami5001/gantt-charter" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">repository</a>,
        create a feature branch, and open a pull request with a clear description. Small, focused PRs are the easiest to review.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Improving the web app?</strong> It lives in the <code>site/</code> folder:
        <code>cd site &amp;&amp; npm install &amp;&amp; npm run dev</code>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Improving the Python CLI?</strong> Install the requirements and run the test suite
        with <code>pytest</code> before opening your PR.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The full contribution guidelines are in the
      <a href="https://github.com/sami5001/gantt-charter#contributing" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">repository README</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      No accounts, no uploads, no analytics. Your project data exists only in your browser.
      Details in the <a href={`${base}/guide/`}>guide</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Licence and acknowledgements</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Released under the <a href="https://github.com/sami5001/gantt-charter/blob/main/LICENSE" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">MIT licence</a>.</li>
      <li>Colour palettes from the University of Oxford colour system, via the companion <a href="https://github.com/sami5001/oxford-plotly-theme" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Oxford Plotly Theme</a>.</li>
      <li>Type set in <a href="https://github.com/IBM/plex" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IBM Plex</a> (SIL Open Font License), embedded in exports.</li>
      <li>Built with <a href="https://astro.build" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Astro</a>, React and Tailwind CSS; PDF export via jsPDF and svg2pdf.js.</li>
    </ul>
  </main>
</Layout>
